   "source": [
    "The correlation matrix reveals that **no single indicator carries strong linear signal against the 20-day forward return**. Volume shows the largest association at r ≈ +0.09, followed by Volatility_7d (+0.06), with the remaining features all sitting at or below |r| = 0.02 (RSI_14 ≈ 0.00, MACD −0.01, MACD_Signal −0.01, Daily_Return −0.01). None of these magnitudes are practically meaningful — each indicator explains, at best, on the order of one percent of the variance in `Future_Return_20d`.\n",
    "\n",
    "The off-diagonal block between MACD and MACD_Signal remains strongly positive (r ≈ +0.95) by construction, since MACD_Signal is a 9-period EMA of MACD itself. Both observations directly shape the ML pipeline below. Because no raw indicator is individually useful, the team engineers additional features — multi-horizon returns (Return_3d / 7d / 14d / 30d), log returns, price-vs-moving-average ratios, multi-window volatilities, and z-scored volume — to give the model more chances to detect a useful combination. And because pairs like MACD/MACD_Signal are nearly collinear, a linear classifier would have unstable coefficients; the team therefore reaches for a Random Forest, which is robust to multicollinearity and can recover non-linear interactions a single Pearson correlation cannot detect."
