    "We define:\n",
    "- Target = 1 if the future 20-day return is greater than 3%\n",
    "- Target = 0 otherwise\n",
    "\n",
    "Because stock indicators may contain outliers and may not follow a normal distribution, we use the Mann-Whitney U test instead of a traditional two-sample t-test.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Null Hypothesis (H₀):** The distribution of the technical indicator is the same for both target classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Alternative Hypothesis (H₁):** The distribution of the technical indicator differs between the two target classes.\n",
    "\n",
    "After examining earlier relationships between stock indicators and future returns, this method tests whether specific technical indicators have different distributions across the two future-return classes. This helps decide which types of features may be worth engineering and keeping for prediction."
