  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "After evaluating the model's performace we can analyze which features were most important to making accurate predictions. This is a critical step in the model building process because optimizing features allows us to produce more useful and more accurate results. \n",
    "\n",
    "To determine features importance we are going to use permutation importance. This is the process of testing how well our model performs under difference permutaions of the feature set. This allows us to test how an individal feature contributes to the model as a whole to make accurate predictions. Furthermore, we are choosing permutation importance becasue our features are highly correlated (since they are calculated from other features). Traditional feature importance tests like sklearn's feature_importance_ function becomes bias when features are highly correlated, so under these conditions, permutation importance is optimal. "
   ]
  },
